WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:10.100
Put the mall's centre on the map, choose the circle and the precision, then set the shifts and who works them.

2
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:16.470
Settings starts with the mall's circle. Nobody can clock in until its centre is set.

3
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:22.670
Paste the centre as two numbers, or a map link to the mall's pin.

4
00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:30.360
Or stand in the middle of the mall with your phone and choose Use where I am standing.

5
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:37.270
The circle is a hundred metres by default. Make it bigger if far entrances fall outside.

6
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:44.940
Precision needed: a reading less precise than this is refused, so nobody clocks in on a vague signal.

7
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.820
The preview shows the circle around the centre, to scale.

8
00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.940
Save.

9
00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.100
Shifts: when each group works, the grace minutes and the unpaid break.

10
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:04.060
A shift that ends after midnight counts for the day it started.

11
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.160
Who works it: tick the people.

12
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:14.080
Then assign them from a date. Their lateness and overtime follow this shift from then on.
